1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,698
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,698 --> 00:00:05,220
OTTO: Hey! That's not fair! My lamington is gone!

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,641
IVY: Pip saw who took it.

4
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:11,166
OTTO: Big and loud? It was the kookaburra!

5
00:00:11,566 --> 00:00:15,260
IVY: Hmm. The cockatoo is big and loud too.

6
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:19,827
BRAMBLE: Pip swapped loud for screeching. Which bird screeches?

7
00:00:20,227 --> 00:00:24,537
Swap a dull word for a more exact synonym.

8
00:00:24,937 --> 00:00:28,401
Kookaburras don't screech. They laugh.

9
00:00:28,801 --> 00:00:31,875
Cockatoos screech. Loud and sharp.

10
00:00:32,275 --> 00:00:34,471
It's B! The cockatoo.

11
00:00:34,671 --> 00:00:37,043
OTTO: Oh! I picked too fast!

12
00:00:37,443 --> 00:00:38,792
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

13
00:00:40,292 --> 00:00:43,257
IVY: Listen! The kookaburra is laughing!

14
00:00:43,457 --> 00:00:46,060
OTTO: It's glad we didn't blame it!

15
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:52,779
Say it with me. Swap a dull word for a more exact synonym.

16
00:00:53,179 --> 00:00:57,139
Next case: clapping the syllables in our names.

